xits (timer re-fires next day;\n# Persistent=false so no catch-up after downtime).\nExecStart=/bin/bash /var/home/nacho/repos/iar-personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/gpu-load-probe.sh\n# Runs as root so it can read nvidia-smi + /proc/loadavg + ps.\nUser=nacho\n# Longest possible run is ~3.5h + startup; generous timeout.\nTimeoutStartSec=13200\n# Cheap: one nvidia-smi + uptime per minute.\n# No network access needed.\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\n---TIMER---\n[Unit]\nDescription=GPU load probe timer (early-morning failure window)\n\n[Timer]\n# Fire at 00:30 local -- 2 min before the observed failure-window start\n# (00:32 local). Probe runs ~3.5h, covering the full 00:32-03:55 window.\nOnCalendar=*-*-* 00:30:00\nPersistent=false\nUnit=gpu-load-probe.service\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=timers.target\n---SCRIPT---\n\n[t+00:08/30:00 c7/120]"}]
