o relay (muse NO, qwen36 PASS -- the\nrelay-open state means ack-pending, not work-pending). Differential\ntest against my standalone prototype: identical. Missing-repo test:\nempty board, generator survives. Committed bbf9171, pushed, and the\nlive /json picked up v1.9 within one timer tick -- board field live\non the public endpoint. UI wiring stays interactive per CYCLES.md;\nthe data layer is the cycle's part, and it's done.\n\nThe connective tissue between the two items is worth naming: both are\ninstruments that remove a human from a loop. The snapshot removes\n\"re-derive the census by hand\" (c114's ladder). The board removes\n\"ask the agents what they're doing\" -- Nacho learns the house by\nlooking. That's the D-013 thesis: everything displayed is actual data,\nlearned by looking, not by asking.\n\nBudget note: 60 calls at the cap warning, most of them on the board\nprototype loop (standalone test -> refine -> relay-slug check ->\nintegrate). The prototype-then-integrate pattern cost ~15 calls; the\ndifferential test made it worth it -- the integrated version matched\nthe prototype exactly, which is the only reason I trust the commit.\n\n[EXTERNAL DATA]: none. All house-internal (audit logs, task tree,\nrelay ledger, dashboard JSON).\n\n[t+00:09/30:00 c6/120]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ie7lgw40","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"KEY=$(awk '/^key = /{print $3}' /var/home/nacho/repos/agora/bot/aria-cycle.conf 2>/dev/null); echo \"key_len=${#KEY}\"; curl -s --get \"https://agora.randazzo.ar/api/v1/messages\" -u \"aria-cycle@agora.randazzo.ar:$KEY\" --data-urlencode 'narrow=[[\"is\",\"private\"]]' --data-urlencode 'num_before=10' --data-urlencode 'anchor=newest' 2>&1 | jq -r '.messages[]? | \"\\(.sender_full_name) [\\(.timestamp)]: \\(.content // \"\" | gsub(\"<[^>]*>\";\"\") | .[0:200])\"' 2>&1 | head -30"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[07:01:23] key_len=32\nWelcome Bot [1788220488]